[{"id":3330940683,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7Gih8L","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2308167?u=f7f8e0273f784f5ec6f6b7fe4a88d449896eb48a&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Ivorforce","id":2308167,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjIzMDgxNjc=","login":"Ivorforce","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Ivorforce"},"body":"While reducing the effects of `ClassDB` on compile time performance is a great goal, I'm not sure about the approach taken here (and the previous PR). I think this becomes more clear when we think about the implications of merging this PR:\r\n\r\nIf we decide the eventual goal is to remove automatic inclusion of the binding methods from the headers, we'll have to accept that every single `.cpp` file for an `Object` subclass that binds methods (i.e. all of them?) will have to include the binder headers explicitly.\r\nFrom a quick glance, that's 900 files. That's a lot of work, and a lot of added includes. And in the end, every single Object subclass `.cpp` file will still include `ClassDB` because it needs to register its bindings to it. There might be some compile units that no longer need to include `ClassDB`, but I have a feeling it wouldn't be enough to be worth it.\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, that makes the `ClassDB` include problem a bit difficult. I don't have a good idea for a solution yet, but I'm not sure it will be as straightforward here as to try to reduce how many headers include it, because it will end up in most compile units anyway.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111573#pullrequestreview-3330940683","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111573","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2025-10-13T10:37:52Z"},{"id":3869474896,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mo4BQ","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?u=34072b401722100a7c0c0d61e37b376cf22b4545&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","login":"Repiteo","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo"},"body":"A very good start! Glad the churn of noisy `class_db.h` includes is largely taken care of, though it definitely reveals noise elsewhere (an inevitability).","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111573#pullrequestreview-3869474896","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111573","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-27T23:17:32Z"},{"id":3869542395,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mpIf7","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/41305715?u=a27600b43b5278ada0f7abc144fcb1b615bdef8e&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/StarryWorm","id":41305715,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQxMzA1NzE1","login":"StarryWorm","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/StarryWorm"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/111573#pullrequestreview-3869542395","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/111573","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-27T23:27:10Z"},{"id":3869553521,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mpLNx","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubus